{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":218774,"duration_api_ms":216963,"num_turns":44,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1a9116e9-88a6-4b59-8532-21c4c05b7555","total_cost_usd":2.06694875,"usage":{"input_tokens":37,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82759,"cache_read_input_tokens":2701840,"output_tokens":7944,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":82759},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":37,"outputTokens":7944,"cacheReadInputTokens":2701840,"cacheCreationInputTokens":82759,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.06694875,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `calibrate_vs06` (validation_suite.rs ~line 2050-2056), `final_algae_total / initial_algae_total` and `final_plant / initial_plant` are used as arguments to `classify_field_f64` with no guard against division-by-zero. If a future change sets initial plant or algae biomass to 0.0, this produces NaN/Infinity which `classify_field_f64` maps to a Fail status but with a misleading detail message. Add a guard or use `FieldCheck::observed_only` when the denominator is zero.","rationale":"Division-by-zero is a latent correctness bug. The current setup values happen to be non-zero, but the code doesn't enforce this invariant. If someone changes the scenario initialization, the report would silently produce a fail with a confusing 'non-finite' error message rather than a clear explanation."},{"body":"The `finalize_custom_row` function (validation_suite.rs ~line 286-298) calls `run.persist_artifacts()` when the checkpoint status is not Pass, and then calls `run.finish()` which internally calls `write_artifacts()` again for the same failure directory. This double-writes all artifact files (metadata.json, checkpoints.json, trace.jsonl, etc.) to the same path, wasting I/O. Either skip `finish()` or skip `persist_artifacts()` for failing runs to avoid the redundant write.","rationale":"On failing scenarios, every artifact file is written twice to the same location. While not a correctness bug (the second write simply overwrites the first), it doubles the I/O work for failure cases. More importantly, the `persist_artifacts()` call captures the state at the time of field checking, while `finish()` writes the state at finalization — if any state mutation happened between these two calls (though none currently does), the second write would silently overwrite the first with different data."},{"body":"The `ComparisonReport::compare()` method (calibration.rs ~line 319) only iterates scenarios from the 'before' report, so scenarios that are new in the 'after' report (e.g., when a new validation scenario is added) are silently dropped from the comparison. The comparison should also report scenarios that appear only in the 'after' report, since adding new scenarios between calibration runs is a realistic workflow.","rationale":"The acceptance criteria states 'Two reports from different parameter sets can be compared: same scenario_id rows are aligned, changes in pass/fail status are highlighted.' When a new scenario is added, it has no 'before' status, but the comparison should still surface it (e.g., as 'new: pass' or 'new: fail') rather than silently omitting it. Without this, users comparing a pre-addition report to a post-addition report get no visibility into the new scenario's status."}],"summary":"Reviewed the calibration-report workflow diff (~1700 lines across 8 files). The implementation is well-structured: `run_calibration_suite` drives all 8 validation scenarios through the shared harness, produces machine-readable JSON with pass/marginal/fail classification per checkpoint, includes artifact paths for failures, and supports cross-run comparison via `ComparisonReport`. The `calibration_report` binary provides a clean CLI entry point. Tests cover report structure, marginal classification, artifact paths, comparison, harness integration, and full workflow with CI timing constraint. Found three issues: (1) unguarded division by initial biomass values in calibrate_vs06 that would produce NaN if setup values become zero, (2) double artifact write in finalize_custom_row for failing scenarios, (3) ComparisonReport silently drops scenarios that only appear in the 'after' report."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f6e84902-dbc8-4f28-b36f-9b8ab38acf6c"}
